**Never** define a status, tone, icon or severity mapping in code comments, a new constant, or a new document. Add it to the dictionary first, then implement.

## Architecture (fixed)

- GitHub Pages → Airtable from the browser. No backend, proxy, worker, server or new service.
- App: `index.html` (UI and logic), `kontroll.html` (driver entry), `storage.airtable.js` (the only Airtable layer), `sw.js`, manifests, `icons/`. No build step, no framework, no npm dependencies in the app.
- Design system: `project/` (tokens, brand book, components in `components/bundle.js` under the `Bilpark` namespace).

## Folder structure

```
Biloversikt-main/               the app (repository)
  index.html                    UI + logic; new code goes next to the code it belongs to
  kontroll.html                 driver entry (same app)
  storage.airtable.js           Airtable only; bump versjon + ?v= on every change
  sw.js                         bump CACHE_VERSION when app-shell files change
  AIRTABLE_MIGRATION.md         update on every field change
  CLAUDE.md · ROADMAP.md · CHANGELOG.md
Dv4/project/                    design system (this documentation)
  *.md                          brand book and specifications (max 24 sections)
  tokens.json                   tokens
  components/<Name>/README.md   component guideline
  components/<Name>/preview.html
  components/bundle.js · bundle.css · index.d.ts
```

Do not add files to the app repository without a reason recorded in `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Allowed components

Build every screen from these, in this order of preference:

1. Foundations: `Icon`, `Button`, `StatusBadge`, `Card`, `KpiCard`, `VehicleCard`, `DataTable`.
2. Fleet Operations: `AppShell`, `Sidebar`, `OperationalHeader`, `FilterChip`, `FleetHealthOverview`, `ComplianceCard`, `FollowUpSummary`, `FollowUpRow`, `FollowUpPanel`, `AlertCard`, `WorkshopCard`, `WorkshopScheduler`, `VehicleTimeline`, `CaseCard`, `CalendarEvent`, `ActivityFeed`, `LinkDialog`.
3. States: `EmptyState`, `LoadingState`, `ErrorState`, `StaleDataIndicator`.
4. DriverControl: `DriverHeader`, `QuickActions`, `InspectionWizard`, `DamageWizard`, `PhotoCapture`, `SyncStatus`, `OfflineBanner`.

`VehicleHealth` is not a new chrome: it is statusrad + §4 chips on the vehicle profile. Do not add a second health score.

A new component is allowed only when none of these can carry the content, and only after its README (purpose, states, accessibility, tokens) exists in `project/components/`.

## Forbidden

- Third-party UI kits, calendar or chart libraries with their own styling.
- A second icon set, emoji in the UI, hand-drawn SVG icons. Lucide only.
- Cards with a coloured left border; gradients other than the hero gradient; glow, neon, glossy effects.
- `storage.set()` on a list table from DriverControl offline code (it deletes rows; use `upsertRow`).
- Deleting a booking, damage, control or case from the UI (change status instead).
- Charts, trends or sparklines above `FleetHealthOverview`.
- Merging Flåtehelse, Operativ etterlevelse and Verkstedoppfølging into one card or one percentage.
- Workshop follow-up that books, auto-closes cases, or sets Driftsstatus to `aktiv`.
- Any metric about a person (see the KPI framework).
- Reading or writing retired fields (`Vehicles.Status`, `AktiveSaker.Priority`).

## Naming conventions

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Stored status value | lowercase kebab, Norwegian, from the dictionary | `kan-ikke-brukes`, `pagar` |
| Airtable column | PascalCase Norwegian (existing style) | `Driftsstatus`, `ForventetFerdig` |
| App field (`LIST_TABLES` key) | camelCase of the column | `driftsstatus`, `forventetFerdig` |
| App functions | Norwegian, descriptive, existing style | `vehicleHovedstatus()`, `sakErApen()`, `flatehelse()` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE, Norwegian | `EU_KONTROLL_VARSEL_DAGER_HASTER` |
| Design-system components | PascalCase English | `WorkshopCard` |
| Settings keys | lowercase kebab; per-item keys `prefix:<id>` | `standard-nedetid`, `synkstatus:<enhetId>` |
| UI text | Norwegian bokmål, sentence case, «du», no exclamation marks | «Neste verksted» |

## Design tokens (V4)

**Main rule:** the V4 tokens are the authoritative design source. They are defined once in `:root` at the top of `index.html`, with values identical to `tokens.json` (see `visual-language-v4.md` and `V4_TOKEN_MIGRATION.md`). Every new component, new screen, new CSS rule and new design change uses the V4 tokens **directly**. The transition aliases exist only for backwards compatibility and are never used in new code.

### Required V4 token set

| Group | Tokens |
|---|---|
| Background and surfaces | `--bg`, `--surface`, `--surface-elevated` |
| Text | `--ink`, `--ink-muted` |
| Border | `--border`, `--border-strong` |
| Interaction | `--hover`, `--accent`, `--on-accent` |
| Status | `--success` / `--success-soft`, `--warning` / `--warning-soft`, `--danger` / `--danger-soft`, `--danger-strong` / `--on-danger`, `--info` / `--info-soft`, `--workshop` / `--workshop-soft`, `--neutral` / `--neutral-soft` |
| Radius | `--radius-sm`, `--radius-md`, `--radius-lg`, `--radius-pill` |
| Shadows | `--shadow-card`, `--shadow-overlay` |

The token block also holds `--surface-gradient-start` / `--surface-gradient-end` (the fleet-health hero only), `--font-sans`, `--space-1` … `--space-12` and `--icon-table` / `--icon-standard` / `--icon-nav` / `--icon-kpi`. Use them in the same way.

### Forbidden variables in new code

Do **not** introduce new references to:

```
--surface-2   --surface-3   --ink-2   --muted
--line        --line-soft
--red         --red-soft
--amber       --amber-soft
--green       --green-soft   --green-ink
--orange      --orange-soft
--blue        --blue-soft
--chrome-bg   --chrome-text
--radius
--sh-card     --sh-hover
```

These are transition aliases and are phased out during the migration. `--purple`, `--teal` and `--plate-blue` have no V4 equivalent and are being removed; never use them in new code either.

### CSS rules

- Never use a hard-coded colour value when a matching token exists.
- Never add new hex colours in components. Hex values live only in the V4 token block.
- Never add a new local colour variable when a matching V4 token exists.
- Never add a new local design token for colour, border, radius or shadow when a matching V4 token already exists.
- Never add a new shadow literal when a matching V4 token exists (`--shadow-card`, `--shadow-overlay`).
- Never add a new radius literal when a matching V4 token exists (`--radius-sm` / `-md` / `-lg` / `-pill`).
- Spacing, type and icon sizes come from the token scales; no one-off pixel values in new code.

### Focus style

- Focus styles use `outline: 2px solid var(--accent);` with `outline-offset: 2px`.
- Do not use your own focus colours.
- Do not introduce alternative focus styles without an explicit design decision.

### Status system

- Status is always represented with the six tones `success`, `warning`, `danger`, `info`, `workshop` and `neutral`. Which tone a status gets comes from the status dictionary.
- Do not create new concept colours.
- Do not create parallel status systems.
- Do not introduce new status colours without an explicit decision.

### Migration rule

- W0 established the V4 tokens as the new visual truth.
- The aliases exist only to allow gradual migration of existing code.
- The aliases are phased out during W1–W10 (`v4-foundation-migration.md`).
- New code is never built on the aliases.
- New code is written as if the aliases do not exist.

## State handling

Every data-driven view or component must implement:

| State | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Loading | `LoadingState` skeleton shaped like the content; never zeros; label after 6 s; `ErrorState` after 20 s |
| Empty | `EmptyState` with `verifiedAt`, only with fresh data |
| Error | `ErrorState` scoped to the failing section, with last good time and retry |
| Offline / stale | Last known values + `StaleDataIndicator`; `EmptyState stale` for empty lists; writes disabled in admin, queued in DriverControl |

Plus the component's own states from `component-states.md`. A pull request that adds a view without all four is incomplete.

Status values come from the stored field or the dictionary's derivation function, never from a string typed in a template.

## Data rules (from CLAUDE.md, repeated because they break things)

- A new Airtable field is added to `LIST_TABLES` in the same change that starts using it, and to `airtable-schema-v2.md` and `AIRTABLE_MIGRATION.md`.
- `v.km` is the only authoritative km; it is never lowered.
- Every stored-status change appends to `StatusHistorikk`; never rewrite history.
- Rules that depend on time run in the day-boundary pass (`handhevOperativtDogn()`), not in timers.
- Dual writes during migration: `UteAvDrift` with `Driftsstatus`, `Utfort` with `Status`.

## Responsiveness

- Works at 375 px wide: 16 px side gutter, no horizontal page scroll, cards stack to one column in blueprint order.
- Two-column layouts from 1024 px.
- Touch targets ≥ 48 × 48 px; DriverControl QuickActions and wizard answers ≥ 64 px tall.
- Test desktop, mobile and DriverControl after every relevant change (CLAUDE.md).

## Accessibility

- Status is never colour alone: icon + word (`StatusBadge` does this).
- Visible focus ring: 2 px `accent`, 2 px offset, on every interactive element.
- Contrast: body text ≥ 4.5:1; focus ring and icons ≥ 3:1. `neutral` is never used for text.
- Real buttons and links; clickable cards are buttons with an accessible name.
- `role="alert"` only on Critical `AlertCard` and `ErrorState`; `role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"` on stale and empty states.
- Honour `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Form fields have labels; errors are text next to the field.

## Before you finish

- [ ] No new status, tone, icon or severity outside the dictionary.
- [ ] No hardcoded colour, shadow or radius literal where a V4 token exists.
- [ ] No new reference to a transition alias (`--line`, `--muted`, `--red` … see «Forbidden variables in new code»).
- [ ] Focus = `2px solid var(--accent)`, offset 2 px.
- [ ] Four universal states implemented.
- [ ] Works at 375 px.
- [ ] `LIST_TABLES`, schema doc and migration doc updated for any field change; `versjon` and `?v=` bumped; `CACHE_VERSION` bumped if the app shell changed.
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` updated.
